## b. Continuous Integration Rules

| Workflow Stage | CI Rule / Standard | Operational Requirement |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Branch Strategy** | Isolated Feature Branches | All new features and fixes must be developed using a separate `feature/*` branch. |
| **Branch Protection** | Restricted Direct Access | Developers must not directly push changes to the `main` or `dev` branches. |
| **Code Integration** | Pull Request Gate | Completed features must be submitted through a Pull Request to the `dev` branch. |
| **Peer Approval** | Minimum Review Threshold | Each Pull Request must be reviewed by at least one other team member before merging. |
| **Automation** | Triggered CI Checks | CI checks must run automatically when code is pushed to a feature branch or when a Pull Request is created or updated. |
| **Build & Test** | Build Verification | CI must verify that the project can be built successfully and that automated tests, where available, pass successfully. |
| **Quality Gate** | Zero-Failure Merge Policy | Code that fails the required CI checks must not be merged until the errors are fixed. |
| **Staging** | Staging & Integration Branch | The `dev` branch is used to integrate and test completed features before they are released to `main`. |
| **Production** | Stable Release Baseline | The `main` branch must contain only stable and production-ready code. |
| **System Health** | Regression Safeguards | Changes merged into `dev` should not break existing system modules such as Customer, Staff, Product, and Order functions. |
| **Code Quality** | Style Compliance | Developers should ensure that their code follows the approved naming conventions and modularity rules before creating a Pull Request. |
| **Function Length** | Modularity Limits | Functions should remain within the agreed maximum of 30 lines unless there is a documented reason for exceeding the limit. |
| **Defect Triage** | Ownership & Resolution | Any failed CI build or test should be investigated and resolved by the developer responsible for the change. |
